---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy & HIPAA Notice">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 space-y-8 prose text-stone-800">
    <div class="space-y-2 border-b border-stone-200 pb-6">
      <span class="badge-reviewed">Legal & Compliance</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-[#1B4332]">Privacy Policy & Notice of Privacy Practices</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-stone-500">Effective Date: January 1, 2025 | Last Reviewed: January 15, 2025</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Website Data Privacy Overview</h2>
    <p>
      At Dr. Ameena Endocrinology & Metabolic Care, we respect your right to personal and medical privacy. This Website Privacy Policy explains how information is handled on doctorameena.com.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Zero Collection of Protected Health Information (PHI) via Tools</h2>
    <p>
      All interactive web applications on doctorameena.com—including the <strong>Symptom Checklist</strong>, <strong>Visit Question Builder</strong>, and <strong>Insurance Checker</strong>—execute entirely within your web browser's local computational memory (JavaScript engine). No answers, symptom selections, or personal health choices are transmitted to, recorded by, or stored on our web server or any external third-party database.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Form Submissions & Email Communication</h2>
    <p>
      Inquiry and appointment request forms on this website collect basic administrative details (name, email, phone number, preferred appointment time) strictly for practice scheduling purposes. Please do not transmit sensitive personal health details, urgent medical symptoms, or confidential psychiatric history through unencrypted web forms.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Web Analytics & Cookie Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This website utilizes minimal, privacy-focused web analytics that do not track users across external websites or store personally identifiable tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Notice of HIPAA Privacy Practices</h2>
    <p>
      In-office clinical care at Dr. Ameena's Austin practice is governed by the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA). Patients receive a formal Notice of Privacy Practices during in-person intake detailing how protected health information (PHI) is safeguarded in electronic health records (EHR).
    </p>

    <div class="disclaimer-box">
      <strong>Questions Regarding Privacy Practices:</strong> If you have questions regarding privacy or data handling, please contact our administrative office at (512) 555-0199 <span class="bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 text-xs px-1 rounded font-bold">[NEEDS CONFIRMATION]</span> or 1200 Medical Parkway, Suite 400, Austin, TX 78756.
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
